---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Method — GrabStack" description="Who makes GrabStack, and how we judge.">
  <section class="py-6 sm:py-10">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
      Method<span class="text-accent">.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-xl text-sm text-muted">
      Who makes GrabStack, and how we judge.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="space-y-8">
    <!-- Identity -->
    <section class="rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-surface p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-paper">Who</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper/80">
        GrabStack is an independent field guide to AI tools, agents and stacks. It exists because
        the space moves fast, most directories rot, and honest assessment is rare. We're not
        venture-backed, we carry no affiliate links, and we say when something is overhyped.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Methodology -->
    <section id="methodology" class="scroll-mt-24 rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-surface p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-paper">How we judge</h2>
      <div class="mt-2 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper/80">
        <p>
          Every tool in GrabStack carries a status, a dated claim, and a review-by date. We
          evaluate based on real-world utility, benchmark performance where available, community
          adoption, and whether the tool actually ships updates.
        </p>
        <p>
          We include adjacent, non-AI tools when they're part of a working stack — the goal is the honest picture, not a purity test.
        </p>
        <p>
          When a tool dies, gets acquired, or quietly stops mattering, we move it to
          <a href="/cemetery" class="text-accent hover:underline">The Cemetery</a> rather than
          deleting it. Honest records matter more than clean catalogues.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Update cadence -->
    <section class="rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-surface p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-paper">Update cadence</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper/80">
        Every entry has a review-by date. When that date passes, the entry is flagged for review.
        <a href="/wire" class="text-accent hover:underline">The Wire</a> publishes dated field
        reports as things change. The goal is freshness, not volume.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
